# Manual tests for the Grocery List API.
# Run them from Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client extension) while the API is running.
# Execute "register" (or "login" if the user already exists) first: the token is reused by the other requests.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5248
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jdoe",
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Log in
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jdoe",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Get the grocery list of the logged-in user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/grocery-items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a product
# @name addItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/grocery-items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Milk"
}

### Tag the product (put it in the basket)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/grocery-items/{{addItem.response.body.$.id}}/tag
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Un-tag the product (put it back on the shelf)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/grocery-items/{{addItem.response.body.$.id}}/untag
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Remove the product
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/grocery-items/{{addItem.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token the list is not accessible (expected: 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/grocery-items
